Rosemary ice cream is not something that jumps out at me as a flavour i would like, but....... if you don't try, you'll never know!

So if you want to try and make this plant based Rosemary ice cream, this is what you'll need:

700g Cashew milk
500g Plant cream @ 31% fat ish
370g Plant Based Condensed Milk
100g Sugar
50g Dextrose
1.5g Stabilizer (optional but recommended)
Handful of fresh Rosemary cut and crushed. 

Now there are lot's of different ty[es of rosemary it appears so use what you can. 

